        {
            "id": "7d3994d2-d2c6-476a-b231-5d24618097c0",
            "build_id": "2c330e7b-b493-4618-99e8-36d31ba2e7ec",
            "round_number": 4,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-07-20T15:49:33.780192+00:00",
            "notes": "This is when you should start investing into weapon power, because I found that additional attack speed past 50% stops becoming useful if you don't have the damage per shot to back it up. [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) should do for now. Try to keep attack speed to a minumum of 40%. Get [Booster Jets](item_a291de85-b6d9-43cf-b5da-f3184a156f48) to do it, but if you can't afford it then keep the [Wrist Wraps](item_19183386-c859-42ca-93f2-355d47d01e36) and  [Aftermarket Firing Pin](item_2485b212-b286-42d0-a2bd-20eb4396b054). There's also a few items that you already have and can get at this stage that scales with weapon damage effectively, including the aforementioned [Aerial Distresser](item_0fcb9020-c729-49b9-b398-3223797b6204).\n\nYou may also notice at this point that you're getting ult charge FAST. I had a game where I was going against a Sigma running the unkillable build and in the final round I pulled off 3 ults while the enemy Sigma only pulled off one, and he used it as soon as he got it, too.\n\nBetter capitalize on this ult charge. [Maglev Multiplier](item_a842eb8b-983b-4560-9af6-923776a2a2a8) combined with your [Aerial Distresser](item_0fcb9020-c729-49b9-b398-3223797b6204) makes your ult extremely deadly, with the caveat that you become more vulnerable to being stunned out of ult. The extended ult time can be fairly useful against enemies with invincibility abilities if used correctly as their invincibility abilities end while they're still caught in your ult.\n\n[Vanadium Injection](item_57953fbc-11ff-4e92-9928-fc59b7be668f) could be good, though I haven't tested it out as I tend to be proactive in using my ult.",
